<!--
  Lint configuration for the :app module.

  InvalidFragmentVersionForActivityResult
  ========================================
  Lint reports app/src/main/java/com/example/MainActivity.kt:91
      registerForActivityResult(ActivityResultContracts.RequestPermission()) { ... }
  with "Upgrade Fragment version to at least 1.3.0." Lint treats this as a Fatal-severity
  issue, so it fails `assembleRelease` (via lintVitalRelease) while never affecting
  `assembleDebug`, which is why it only showed up once release builds were introduced.

  It is a false positive in this project:
    * MainActivity extends androidx.activity.ComponentActivity, which implements
      ActivityResultCaller itself (androidx.activity 1.10.1). No Fragment is involved,
      so there is no Fragment-version-related crash risk on any supported API level.
    * The project has no androidx.fragment dependency at all, so lint cannot resolve a
      Fragment version and falls back to treating it as older than 1.3.0.

  Adding an unused androidx.fragment dependency purely to satisfy this version check would
  ship dead weight in every APK, so the check is ignored instead. Delete this entry if the
  app ever starts using Fragments.
-->
<lint>
    <issue id="InvalidFragmentVersionForActivityResult" severity="ignore" />
</lint>
